     left than Layer 2's so the wider box still lands inside the same
     safe margin from the viewport edge, verified at 1366px and 1440px.
     Placed lower on the stage, over the bottom layer's own right-front
     face, clear of its circuit-node glints. Gated the same way as its
     hotspot and glow: hidden through Layer 2's own reveal, shown only
     once its own trigger has been pressed. */
  .dy-hero__reveal--layer3 {
    left: 78%;
    top: 74%;
    /* Narrowed from 38% for the same reason as Layer 2's box above —
       this one overshot the stage's right edge by ~102px at 640px
       stage width against a real margin of only ~84–86px, clipping
       "…ACT FOR YOU" by several pixels at exactly 1366/1440px. 33%
       holds a genuine safety margin across the whole 981–1699px range
       (the ≥1700px wide variant below repositions this off-stage
       anyway, where it already had generous room). */
    width: 33%;
    max-width: 266px;
  }

  /* Same gap as the glow's above: the base `[data-reveal='1']
     .dy-hero__reveal` rule matches this panel too, so without its own
     override here it would show up as soon as Layer 1 opens instead of
     waiting for Layer 2. */
  [data-reveal='1'] .dy-hero__reveal--layer3 {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(6px);
  }

  [data-reveal2='1'] .dy-hero__reveal--layer3 {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(6px);
  }

  [data-reveal3='1'] .dy-hero__reveal--layer3 {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }

  /* The single continuation trigger: it only ever makes sense once the
     discovery sequence has run its full course, so it sits directly
     under Layer 3's own text, anchored at the same left edge so the
     whole column — three reveals plus this closing line — reads as one
     piece. Hidden by default and only ever brought in by data-reveal3;
     no earlier state shows it. Styled as a smaller, quieter echo of the
     primary .dy-hero__cta pill (same ink fill, saffron circular arrow,
     999px radius, hover lift) so it reads as the payoff of the
     sequence rather than a new component vocabulary — just scaled
     down and lighter so it stays subordinate to the hero's own CTA. */
  .dy-hero__continue {
    position: absolute;
    left: 78%;
    top: 92%;
    width: fit-content;
    max-width: 266px;
    margin: 0;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 5px 5px 5px 14px;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.006em;
    white-space: nowrap;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 18px rgba(17, 21, 28, 0.12);
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(6px);
    transition: opacity 420ms ease, transform 420ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease;
    pointer-events: none;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .dy-hero__continue:disabled {
    cursor: default;
  }

  [data-reveal3='1'] .dy-hero__continue {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
    pointer-events: auto;
  }

  [data-reveal3='1'] .dy-hero__continue:hover {
    box-shadow: 0 12px 24px rgba(17, 21, 28, 0.18);
  }

  [data-reveal3='1'] .dy-hero__continue:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--cobalt);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .dy-hero__continue span {
    flex: none;
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--saffron);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 11px;
  }

  /* =========================================================
     REALIZATION STATE
     Reached only by activating the (already-wired) continue CTA,
     which sets data-realized="1" on the stage. Nothing here changes
     layout — every rule below is opacity/veil only, so the stage
     keeps its exact footprint whether or not this state is active.
     Deliberately a single quiet fade: one duration, one easing, no
     staggering, no new artwork or copy — just the discovery layer
     receding so a simpler moment can follow later.
     ========================================================= */

  /* The veil itself: transparent over the seated human's own portion
     of the artwork (left ~40%), easing to a translucent cream wash —
     the page's own background tone — over the AI counterpart and the
     three layers, so they read as "still there, now background"
     rather than erased. */
  .dy-hero__realize-scrim {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    left: 40%;
    background: linear-gradient(
      to right,
      rgba(248, 245, 239, 0) 0%,
      rgba(248, 245, 239, 0.82) 24%,
      rgba(248, 245, 239, 0.82) 100%
    );
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    transition: opacity 650ms ease;
  }

  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__realize-scrim {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  /* Once the visitor brings the story back to the AI, the veil eases
     back — the human, the AI counterpart and the three layers return
     to clearer presence, without fully restoring the original scene
     (the speech bubbles, cards and hotspots stay retired). Same
     specificity as the rule above; living after it in the sheet is
     what lets this win once both realized and advance are true. */
  [data-advance='1'] .dy-hero__realize-scrim {
    opacity: 0.32;
  }

  /* An extra, layers-only recession on top of the shared veil above —
     starts to the right of the AI counterpart (never over it, and
     never over the human), so the technology layers specifically
     quiet down into atmospheric context once the final realization
     arrives. Soft-edged fade-in rather than a hard vertical seam. The
     realization text sits directly on this — no background of its
     own — so this is what actually carries its readability. */
  .dy-hero__final-layer-fade {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    left: 52%;
    background: linear-gradient(
      to right,
      rgba(248, 245, 239, 0) 0%,
      rgba(248, 245, 239, 0.6) 16%,
      rgba(248, 245, 239, 0.6) 100%
    );
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    transition: opacity 700ms ease 250ms;
  }

  [data-advance='1'] .dy-hero__final-layer-fade {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  /* Everything that belonged to the discovery journey itself — the
     exchange bubbles, the consequence cards/chips, all three saffron
     cues and their connecting thread, and the three reveal texts —
     steps out of the way once that journey is done. Same treatment,
     same timing, across all of them; explicit per-modifier selectors
     (mirroring the layer2/layer3 gating above) so specificity ties
     resolve correctly regardless of source order. */
  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__bubble,
  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__card--pay,
  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__chip--calendar,
  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__chip--confirmation,
  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__discovery,
  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__discovery-hotspot,
  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__discovery-hotspot--layer2,
  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__discovery-hotspot--layer3,
  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__reveal-glow,
  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__reveal-glow--layer2,
  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__reveal-glow--layer3,
  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__reveal,
  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__reveal--layer2,
  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__reveal--layer3,
  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__continue {
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    transition: opacity 500ms ease;
  }

  /* The realization's opening line: editorial, not a UI element — no
     card, no border, no background. Moved up into the top of the
     right-side realization canvas — not leftover space around the
     faded layers, but the head of a composition that still needs
     room below it for the key visual, its explanation, and the
     eventual realization copy, none of which exist yet. Kept clear
     of the seated human and the AI counterpart's face. A small
     saffron rule stands in for the discovery cues above it, just
     enough to lead the eye in without reintroducing the hotspot
     vocabulary. Fades up slightly after the scrim so it reads as the
     thought that follows the recession, not simultaneous with it. */
  .dy-hero__realize-thought {
    position: absolute;
    left: 58%;
    top: 8%;
    width: 40%;
    max-width: 300px;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(8px);
    transition: opacity 600ms ease 150ms, transform 600ms ease 150ms;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .dy-hero__realize-thought::before {
    content: '';
    display: block;
    width: 22px;
    height: 2px;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--saffron);
  }

  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__realize-thought {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }

  /* The key visual: sits directly under/around the sentence rather
     than in a card of its own — no border, background, or caption.
     Anchored a little left of the text so it spans the width the
     faded AI counterpart and layers occupy, using the photo's own
     transparent hand-side edge to blend into that emptied space
     instead of a hard rectangle. Stays right of the seated human's
     own ~40% and well short of the stage's right/bottom edges, so it
     reads as the focal point of this state without crowding out what
     is still faintly visible behind it. Arrives a beat after the
     sentence — same restrained single-fade language, just a later
     start. */
  .dy-hero__realize-key {
    position: absolute;
    left: 43%;
    top: 27%;
    width: 46%;
    max-width: 320px;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(10px);
    transition: opacity 650ms ease 280ms, transform 650ms ease 280ms;
    pointer-events: none;
    /* The source photo only fades to transparent on its hand side —
       the door/lock side is a hard photographic rectangle. A soft
       radial mask, centred over the key and lock themselves, fades
       every edge of that rectangle into the page instead, so nothing
       here reads as a bordered card or cut-out sticker. */
    mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 58% 58% at 58% 45%, #000 32%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55) 62%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0) 100%);
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 58% 58% at 58% 45%, #000 32%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55) 62%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0) 100%);
  }

  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__realize-key {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }

  /* The second analogy beat's own affordance — plain saffron text plus
     an arrow, no pill/background, so it reads as editorial punctuation
     rather than another UI control. Sits just under the key visual, in
     the same left column as the opening thought. Visible (though still
     disabled — see script) only once the realization state itself
     exists; hidden again the moment it's used, since the two lines it
     reveals take its place. */
  .dy-hero__realize-next {
    position: absolute;
    left: 58%;
    top: 80%;
    width: fit-content;
    max-width: 300px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: none;
    background: none;
    text-align: left;
    color: var(--saffron);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.006em;
    cursor: pointer;
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(6px);
    transition: opacity 500ms ease, transform 500ms ease;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .dy-hero__realize-next:disabled {
    cursor: default;
  }

  .dy-hero__realize-next:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--cobalt);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  [data-realized='1'] .dy-hero__realize-next {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
    pointer-events: auto;
  }

  [data-analogy2='1'] .dy-hero__realize-next {
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  /* The two revealed lines: same editorial serif voice as the opening
     thought, so this reads as the next sentence in one story rather
     than a new component. Clear hierarchy between them — the first is
     set slightly stronger (closer in weight/size to the opening
     thought), the second sits underneath it, smaller and in the
     site's softer ink tone, the way a clarifying clause would in body
     copy. Both stay hidden until the affordance above is pressed, and
     arrive together as one restrained transition — the pair lives in
     a single positioned wrapper with the lines stacked in normal flow
     inside it, so the second line always sits cleanly under the
     first no matter how many lines the first one wraps to. */
  .dy-hero__realize-next-copy {
    position: absolute;
    left: 58%;
    top: 80%;
    width: 42%;
    max-width: 310px;
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(8px);
    transition: opacity 550ms ease, transform 550ms ease;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  [data-analogy2='1'] .dy-hero__realize-next-copy {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
    pointer-events: auto;
  }

  .dy-hero__realize-next-text {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.008em;
  }

  .dy-hero__realize-next-subtext {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: -0.006em;
  }

  /* The bridge line back to the AI agent: a clear paragraph break
     (not just a line break) from the house-key pair above it, and a
     step quieter throughout — smaller than even the house-key
     subtext — so the analogy still leads and this reads as its
     natural continuation rather than a competing thought. */
  .dy-hero__realize-bridge-text {
    margin: 22px 0 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: -0.006em;
  }

  .dy-hero__realize-bridge-subtext {
    margin: 6px 0 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.45;
    letter-spacing: -0.004em;
  }

  /* The closing editorial cue — deliberately not the .dy-hero__cta /
     .dy-hero__continue pill language. No fill, no border, no padding
     box: just near-black text with a small saffron arrow, sitting in
     normal flow under the bridge lines like the next sentence of the
     same paragraph rather than a product control. Disabled (see
     script) until the "And then?" state exists, so it's inert and
     unfocusable before then; the generous top margin is the
     "comfortable whitespace" this needs to read as a pause before
     moving on, not a continuation of the same block. */
  .dy-hero__realize-turn {
    display: inline-block;
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: none;
    background: none;
    text-align: left;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.008em;
    cursor: pointer;
    /* Keeps the saffron circle on the same line as the text instead of
       wrapping onto its own line — the line was just wide enough for
       the sentence alone that adding the inline circle pushed past the
       wrap width. */
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* A small circular action treatment on the arrow only — the same
     saffron-circle language as .dy-hero__cta / .dy-hero__continue's
     own arrows, just at a quieter scale, so this still reads as an
     editorial transition rather than a second primary CTA. Text and
     circle stay one clickable target (both live inside the single
     <button>); the circle is what actually signals "this moves you
     forward" now, so it carries the interactive affordance instead of
     relying on a hover underline alone. */
  .dy-hero__realize-turn span {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    margin-left: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--saffron);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 11px;
    vertical-align: middle;
    transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease;
  }

  .dy-hero__realize-turn:disabled {
    cursor: default;
  }

  /* Subtle on purpose — a page-turn, not a button press: the text
     gets a light underline, the circle a light lift, nothing louder. */
  .dy-hero__realize-turn:hover:not(:disabled) {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .dy-hero__realize-turn:hover:not(:disabled) span {
    transform: scale(1.08);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(232, 117, 36, 0.35);
  }

  .dy-hero__realize-turn:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--cobalt);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  /* The house-key analogy has done its job by this point, so it
     recedes — gently, using each element's own existing fade
     (600–650ms, already set above), not a hard cut. Same specificity
     (attribute + class) as the opacity:1 rules these override, so
     placement after them in the stylesheet is what makes the
     override win. */
  [data-advance='1'] .dy-hero__realize-thought,
  [data-advance='1'] .dy-hero__realize-key,
  [data-advance='1'] .dy-hero__realize-next-copy {
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  /* The layers-only recession that makes the text above readable
     without any background of its own — see .dy-hero__final-layer-fade
     above, which does that work now. Text-shadow and a local
     multiply-darken behind the text were tried first and neither held
     up; a haze/blur card behind the text worked but read as a
     background, which this state should not have at all. */
  .dy-hero__final {
    position: absolute;
    left: 56%;
    top: 26%;
    width: 42%;
    max-width: 300px;
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(10px);
    transition: opacity 700ms ease 320ms, transform 700ms ease 320ms;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  [data-advance='1'] .dy-hero__final {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }

  .dy-hero__final-text {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .dy-hero__final-text::before {
    content: '';
    display: block;
    width: 24px;
    height: 3px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--saffron);
  }

  /* Sits directly beneath the headline — same flow parent, so the
     left edge stays aligned automatically — with just enough gap to
     read as the next line of one editorial block, not a separately
     anchored annotation. Renders straight over the artwork with no
     backdrop of any kind; readability comes only from solid
     foreground contrast (var(--ink), the same near-black as the
     headline, at full opacity, no shadow/glow behind it). */
  .dy-hero__final-support {
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    /* Wider than the headline above it — its own three short lines
       need more room than the headline's two-word-per-line rhythm
       to each land as one line, and there's no other content beside
       it at this depth in the artwork for the extra width to crowd. */
    width: 320px;
    max-width: 34vw;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.6;
    letter-spacing: -0.006em;
  }

  /* WIDE VARIANT: once the stage's own margin past the artwork's right
     edge is reliably wide enough (verified: ~180px clear from ~1700px
     viewport width up, given the -50px group shift), the same
     annotation moves into that clear whitespace instead — off the
     layer, on the page background. It already reads fine there, so the
     cream backing added above for the on-layer default is dropped. */
  @media (min-width: 1700px) {
    .dy-hero__reveal {
      left: 100%;
      /* Was 20% — that put this right on top of the Calendar-updated
         chip (top: 18%, ~29px tall, so it occupies roughly 18–25% of
         the stage's own height): the chip's white pill background was
         painting over this text's first letter. 28% clears the whole
         chip/card cluster above it. */
      top: 28%;
      width: max-content;
      max-width: 172px;
      margin: 0 0 0 14px;
      padding: 0;
      background: none;
      backdrop-filter: none;
      -webkit-backdrop-filter: none;
      mask-image: none;
      -webkit-mask-image: none;
    }

    .dy-hero__reveal-text {
      color: #5a6272;
    }

    /* Layer 2/3 need their own explicit top here (not just width) —
       this media query redeclares `top` on the shared `.dy-hero__reveal`
       base above with a *later* source position, so without their own
       value here they'd silently collapse onto Layer 1's exact spot
       (same specificity, base rule simply wins by appearing later).

       width uses `max-content` (capped by max-width), not `auto`: for
       an absolutely positioned element whose `left` already consumes
       the full containing-block width (left: 100%, inherited from the
       base rule), `width: auto`'s shrink-to-fit calculation collapses
       to the longest *unbreakable* word rather than the full content —
       that's what was rendering these two as a near-single-word-wide
       column of fragments. `max-content` sizes to the full unwrapped
       line first, and max-width still wraps it exactly as intended. */
    .dy-hero__reveal--layer2 {
      top: 50%;
      width: max-content;
      /* 200px was measured against the margin available well past the
         1700px entry point (~230px+), but right at 1700px itself the
         real margin past the stage's own right edge is only ~180px —
         200px plus the 14px left margin above overflowed the viewport
         there. 150px holds inside that tightest case; the text wraps
         an extra line rather than clipping. */
      max-width: 150px;
    }

    .dy-hero__reveal--layer3 {
      top: 72%;
      width: max-content;
      max-width: 150px;
    }
  }

  /* Second consequence: a single quiet line, well short of the paid
     card's weight, stepping down and right from it — still clear of the
     layers' top vertex, and leaving the corner free for the confirmation
     still to come. */
  .dy-hero__chip {
    position: absolute;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 7px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 7px 12.5px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: #fff;
    white-space: nowrap;
    box-shadow: 0 3px 8px rgba(17, 21, 28, 0.06);
  }

  .dy-hero__chip--calendar {
    left: 80.5%;
    top: 18%;
  }

  .dy-hero__chip-icon {
    flex: none;
    width: 15px;
    height: 15px;
    color: var(--cobalt);
  }

  .dy-hero__chip-label {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.004em;
  }

  /* Third and last consequence. The gap between the AI counterpart's arm
     and the layers' own top vertex is the only clear ground left below
     the calendar chip's row — narrow, so this one stays the smallest and
     quietest of the three, tucked well left of Calendar and short of the
     glass. */
  .dy-hero__chip--confirmation {
    left: 50%;
    top: 19%;
    gap: 5px;
    padding: 5px 10px;
    box-shadow: 0 3px 7px rgba(17, 21, 28, 0.05);
  }

  .dy-hero__chip--confirmation .dy-hero__chip-icon {
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
  }

  .dy-hero__chip--confirmation .dy-hero__chip-label {
    font-size: 10.5px;
  }

  .dy-hero__title {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 650px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(54px, 4.4vw, 72px);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 0.94;
    letter-spacing: -0.052em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .dy-hero__title span {
    display: block;
  }

  .dy-hero__title em {
    color: var(--cobalt);
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .dy-hero__intro {
    max-width: 545px;
    margin: clamp(21px, 2.5vh, 27px) 0 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: clamp(17px, 1.25vw, 19px);
    line-height: 1.58;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
  }

  .dy-hero__brandword {
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .dy-hero__subintro {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 12px;
    max-width: 545px;
    margin: clamp(22px, 2.8vh, 30px) 0 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .dy-hero__subintro-icon {
    flex: none;
    width: 24px;
    height: 24px;
    margin-top: 1px;
    color: var(--cobalt);
  }

  .dy-hero__signature {
    display: flex;
    width: fit-content;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    margin: clamp(22px, 2.8vh, 30px) 0 0;
    padding: 12px 20px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .dy-hero__signature-icon {
    flex: none;
